[Better Approach] Sorting and Two Pointers - O(n ^ 3) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is - First, sort the array. Fix the first two elements using two nested loops.For the remaining two elements, use two pointers:Place left after the second fixed element.Place right at the end of the array.If the current sum is equal to x, return true.If the sum is smaller than x, increment left.Otherwise, decrement right.
            C++

    #include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

bool fourSum(vector<int>& arr, int x) {
    int n = arr.size();
    sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());

    // Fix the first two elements.
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 3; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n - 2; j++) {
            int left = j + 1;
            int right = n - 1;

            // Find the remaining two elements using two pointers.
            while (left < right) {
                int sum = arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[left] + arr[right];

                if (sum == x) {
                    return true;
                }

                if (sum < x) {
                    left++;
                } else {
                    right--;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return false;
}

